]

phase('Triple-Verify')
const verified = await pipeline(
  FINDINGS,
  f => parallel(
    ['a', 'b', 'c'].map(() => () =>
      agent(
        `You are independently re-deriving whether a claimed defect in the callisto repo (${WORKSPACE}) is real. Do NOT trust the description below as fact -- read the actual current code/file yourself from scratch and form your own judgment. Two prior independent skeptics already reviewed this claim and did not refute it; your job is a fresh, harder look, including checking whether anything has changed or whether there's a guard/mitigation they missed.

Claimed finding ${f.id} (severity ${f.severity}): "${f.title}"
Location: ${f.file}${f.line ? ':' + f.line : ''}

Read the exact current file content at that location. Confirm whether the defect is real and reachable through the actual public API/CLI/workflow trigger today (not a hypothetical). Also assess: does fixing this in isolation risk breaking something else nearby (note anything you notice, even briefly)?

Report: refuted (bool, default true if you can't find hard evidence), confidence (0-1), evidence (what you actually read), risk_note (one sentence on anything a fix here might disturb, or empty string).`,
        {
