242	      <h1 class="title">How Callisto Ships Software</h1>
243	      <p class="dek">What callisto is, how it's built, and what changed across the last ten pull requests — an adversarial audit of the publish pipeline and the fixes that came out of it.</p>
244	    </header>
245	
246	    <section id="positioning">
247	      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-num">01</span><h2>Where callisto sits</h2></div>
248	      <p class="lede">Release engineering tools answer one question: given a monorepo and a pile of merged PRs, what ships, at what version, to which registry? Callisto's answer is <b>changesets-format intent capture</b> plus a <b>polyglot dependency graph</b> — a combination nothing else in the space offers.</p>
249	
250	      <div class="table-wrap">
251	        <table>
252	          <thead>
253	            <tr><th>Capability</th><th>@changesets/cli</th><th>release-please</th><th>Nx Release</th><th>knope</th><th>callisto</th></tr>
254	          </thead>
255	          <tbody>
256	            <tr><td>Intent format</td><td>Changesets</td><td>Conventional Commits</td><td>Either</td><td>Changesets or commits</td><td class="yes">Changesets (byte-compat)</td></tr>
257	            <tr><td>Cargo workspaces</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓ (plugin)</td><td class="yes">✓ (community)</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="yes">✓ (native)</td></tr>
258	            <tr><td>npm workspaces</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
259	            <tr><td>Cross-ecosystem cascade</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓ (per-ecosystem)</td><td>Partial</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
260	            <tr><td>napi platform-package coordination</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓ (native)</td></tr>
261	            <tr><td>GitHub Release binary assets</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td>Partial</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="no">planned</td></tr>
262	          </tbody>
263	        </table>
264	      </div>
265	      <p style="margin-top:10px; font-size:13.5px;">The niche: teams who like changesets' explicit-intent model but ship a real polyglot monorepo — Rust crates, npm packages, napi native bindings, PyPI wheels — under one version plan.</p>
266	    </section>
267	
268	    <section id="architecture">
269	      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-num">02</span><h2>Crate architecture</h2></div>
270	      <p class="lede">Ten crates, three layers. Layer 1 stays permissively licensed and dependency-free of the rest so it can be embedded anywhere; the engine composes it; the CLI and moon plugin are the only two things a user actually runs.</p>
271	
