353	    <section id="pipeline">
354	      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-num">03</span><h2>The release pipeline</h2></div>
355	      <p class="lede">A release runs as four separate CLI invocations, orchestrated by <code>callisto-action</code> — a GitHub composite action, meaning plain bash gluing calls to the callisto binary together. Each command is a fresh process; there's no shared in-memory state, only the JSON one command prints and the next reads.</p>
356	
357	      <ol class="step-list" style="margin-top:22px;">
358	        <li><span class="step-text"><b><code>plan-publish</code></b> — reads every changeset, walks the dependency graph, computes the cascade, and returns a <code>PublishPlan</code>: exactly which packages bump, to what version, and whether anything is actually pending. Read-only; touches no files, no network.</span></li>
359	        <li><span class="step-text"><b><code>publish</code></b> — takes that plan and shells out to each ecosystem's own publisher (<code>cargo publish</code>, <code>npm publish</code>, <code>twine upload</code>) per package, independently — one package's registry rejection doesn't stop the others. Returns a <code>PublishReport</code>: published, already-published, or failed, per package.</span></li>
360	        <li><span class="step-text"><b><code>filter-plan</code></b> — new in this fix cycle. Takes the original plan plus the report and narrows it down to what the report actually confirms shipped, so a failure upstream can't cost an already-succeeded sibling its tag or release.</span></li>
361	        <li><span class="step-text"><b><code>tag</code></b> — creates one immutable git tag per released package, plus force-moves a floating major-version alias (<code>v1</code>) if requested. Idempotent: re-running against an already-tagged commit is a no-op, not an error.</span></li>
362	      </ol>
