469	    <section id="bigfix">
470	      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-num">06</span><h2>The big fix — #31</h2></div>
471	      <p class="lede">Stacked last on purpose: it's the same file class that caused a real production incident earlier in this effort (the original floating-tag force-push bug). Three findings, one root cause — the shell layer had no reliable way to know <i>which packages actually published</i> or <i>which tags are floating vs. immutable</i>. <a href="https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/31">Currently open, flagged for close review.</a></p>
472	
473	      <h3 style="font-size:16px; margin-top:28px;">Force-push scope</h3>
474	      <div class="compare">
475	        <div class="compare-panel before">
476	          <div class="compare-head">before</div>
477	          <div class="compare-body">callisto tag --plan "$PLAN_JSON" \
478	  --floating-major || true
479	git push origin --tags --force</div>
480	        </div>
481	        <div class="compare-panel after">
482	          <div class="compare-head">after</div>
483	          <div class="compare-body">TAG_REPORT_JSON=$(callisto tag ...)
484	# isFloatingMajor splits the set
485	git push origin "${IMMUTABLE[@]}"
486	git push origin --force "${FLOATING[@]}"</div>
487	        </div>
488	      </div>
489	      <p style="font-size:14px; margin-top:10px;">The blanket force-push clobbered immutable per-version release tags along with the one alias meant to move. <code>|| true</code> hid a real <code>callisto tag</code> failure entirely.</p>
490	
491	      <h3 style="font-size:16px; margin-top:28px;">Empty-plan gating</h3>
492	      <ol class="step-list">
493	        <li><span class="step-text"><b>Before:</b> a docs-only commit after a release still ran artifact placement, publish, tag, and release — reporting <code>published=true</code> for a run that shipped nothing.</span></li>
494	        <li><span class="step-text"><b>After:</b> plan computed once, checked against <code>PublishPlan::is_empty()</code> semantics, everything downstream gated on it.</span></li>
495	      </ol>
496	
497	      <h3 style="font-size:16px; margin-top:28px;">Partial-failure survivors</h3>
498	      <ol class="step-list">
499	        <li><span class="step-text"><b>Before:</b> one package's publish failure killed the step under <code>set -e</code> — already-succeeded siblings never got tagged or released, on every retry, until the failure was fixed.</span></li>
500	        <li><span class="step-text"><b>After:</b> exit code captured, <code>filter-plan</code> narrows the plan to confirmed successes, tag/release run against <i>that</i>, job fails afterward for the real failure.</span></li>
501	      </ol>
502	
503	      <div class="risk-note">Flagged for review, not a quick merge: same file class as the earlier production incident. 8 shell test files, 36 assertions, all green — but shell-script correctness under real GitHub Actions conditions is harder to fully simulate than Rust.</div>
504	    </section>
