{
  "id": "SPEC-RELEASE-LANE-POLICY-006",
  "purpose": "Make release-train, fixed-group, linked-group, prerelease, and stable-release interactions explicit before adding orchestration that could produce competing version authority.",
  "scope": "A normative release-lane policy document at docs/07-lane-policy.md, plus a small set of net-new cross-lane validation checks and planner-determinism codification for the existing version planner (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs). Covers: (a) authoring the lane-authority-precedence documentation (AC-001) and codifying already-shipped fixed/linked-group conflict detection as normative (AC-002) -- these two are pure documentation tracks with no new code; (b) net-new validation logic for prerelease-lane vs. group conflicts (AC-002a) and prerelease-lane-state-gated stable publishes (AC-003), both of which require a new `abandoned: bool` field on `PreState` (crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs) and new rejection paths in the planner; (c) a determinism test asserting `plan_version`'s serialized output is byte-for-byte stable across two consecutive invocations (AC-004), which is independently verifiable and touches no planner internals beyond adding a test -- it stays bundled in this spec as a distinct, self-contained track rather than a separate one.",
  "non_goals": [
    "Implementing a full release-train scheduler or time-based calendar.",
    "Changing existing fixed- or linked-group version semantics without an approved follow-on specification.",
    "Inferring organization-specific release cadence from package names or branch names.",
    "Re-validating or duplicating the fixed/linked-group membership conflict detection already implemented in crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs (GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership, E109).",
    "Introducing a per-package prerelease lane model. The existing prerelease lane (.changeset/pre.json, parsed by callisto_format::parse_pre_json into PreState) is a single workspace-scoped lane whose membership is the packages listed in PreState.initial_versions; this spec documents and constrains that existing model rather than replacing it with a per-package one.",
    "Building any UI, CLI subcommand, or automation for clearing an abandoned prerelease lane. This spec only requires that planning reject an abandoned lane's stable publish with a diagnostic; the operator clears it today via manual edit or deletion of .changeset/pre.json, which is unchanged by this spec."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-001",
      "criterion": "docs/07-lane-policy.md names, for every package at a given planning point, exactly one authority responsible for selecting that package's next version: the package itself (independent lane), its fixed group, its linked group, or the workspace's prerelease lane (as defined by .changeset/pre.json). The document states the precedence for all six unordered pairs among these four authority kinds, with no pairing left undecided: (1) independent x fixed group -- mutually exclusive by construction, since GroupTable::resolve assigns each package to at most one of {ungrouped, fixed_of, linked_of} (crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs); a package cannot simultaneously be independent and a fixed-group member. (2) independent x linked group -- mutually exclusive by the same construction. (3) fixed group x linked group -- mutually exclusive, rejected at config-resolution time per AC-002. (4) independent x prerelease lane -- MAY apply concurrently: an independent package may be listed in PreState.initial_versions; when active, the prerelease lane's mode (PreMode::Pre or PreMode::Exit) takes precedence over independent inference for shaping the package's target version (prerelease tag application or finalization), though the package's own inferred severity still feeds the lane's bump as input. (5) fixed group x prerelease lane -- MUST NOT apply concurrently; rejected per AC-002a. (6) linked group x prerelease lane -- MUST NOT apply concurrently; rejected per AC-002a. The document states as a corollary that a package's prerelease-lane membership can only ever coexist with the independent authority kind, never with fixed or linked group membership, because (5) and (6) are hard rejections.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-002",
      "criterion": "docs/07-lane-policy.md codifies the fixed/linked-group membership conflict detection already implemented in GroupTable::resolve (crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs) as normative: a package listed as a member of two conflicting fixed or linked groups is rejected during config resolution via GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership, with a diagnostic naming the package and both conflicting group names, before any planning proceeds. This criterion documents existing, already-shipped and already-tested behavior (crates/callisto-graph/tests/config_resolve_tests.rs) and requires no new detection logic.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-002a",
      "criterion": "A package that is a member of a fixed or linked group (per GroupTable::fixed_of / GroupTable::linked_of) and is also listed in the active prerelease lane's PreState.initial_versions for the same planning run is unconditionally rejected before manifest, tag, changelog, or registry mutation, with a diagnostic naming the package, the conflicting group name, and the prerelease lane's tag. This is the only conformant behavior -- there is no precedence-based subordination path, and no configuration can make this pairing succeed. This is net-new: no existing code in crates/callisto-graph checks for a prerelease-lane vs. fixed/linked-group conflict; the check is added to plan_version (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs) before cascade planning runs, returning a new GraphError variant.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-003",
      "criterion": "This spec adds a net-new `abandoned: bool` field to PreState (crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs), defaulting to false on deserialization when absent (for backward compatibility with existing pre.json files) and settable only by direct edit of .changeset/pre.json (no CLI support is added by this spec, per non_goals). For a stable-lane publish request (a plan_version invocation not itself running in PreMode::Exit-triggered finalization), the following starting states of the package's prerelease lane determine the outcome: (1) no prerelease lane active -- .changeset/pre.json does not exist -- the stable-lane publish is PERMITTED. (2) prerelease lane active and eligible for promotion -- pre.json exists, the package is in PreState.initial_versions, mode == PreMode::Exit, and abandoned == false -- the stable-lane publish is PERMITTED, and this planning run performs the promotion by finalizing the package's prerelease version to stable (this codifies the already-shipped behavior at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs lines 104-114 as normative, not new logic). (3) prerelease lane active and abandoned -- pre.json exists, the package is in PreState.initial_versions, and abandoned == true (regardless of mode) -- the stable-lane publish is BLOCKED with a diagnostic naming the package and the lane's tag, directing the operator to clear the abandoned lane (delete .changeset/pre.json or edit out the abandoned flag) before planning can proceed for that package. Any other reachable state -- concretely, pre.json exists, the package is in PreState.initial_versions, mode == PreMode::Pre, and abandoned == false, meaning the lane is actively accumulating prereleases and promotion has not been requested -- is a state not enumerated above; a stable-lane publish attempted from it fails planning with a diagnostic naming the package and its current prerelease-lane state (mode=Pre, not yet exited), directing the operator to run the promotion step (transition pre.json to PreMode::Exit) first. An automated test exists for each of the four states above (the three named plus the unenumerated mode==Pre case) asserting the planner's accept/reject decision.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-004",
      "criterion": "Given identical source tree contents, configuration files, and inputs to plan_version (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs), two consecutive invocations of plan_version in the same process produce VersionPlan values whose VersionPlan::to_report() output, serialized via serde_json::to_string (no canonicalization needed, since both outputs originate from the same process and are compared directly rather than hashed across systems), is byte-for-byte identical -- covering both the bumps list (including per-bump ordering) and the diagnostics list (including diagnostic ordering). An automated test in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs runs plan_version twice against one fixture workspace and asserts the two serialized strings are equal.",
      "is_error_case": false
    }
  ],
  "linked_requirement": "REQ-RELEASE-LANE-POLICY"
}

